{"name":"Sunburn","hex":"#b37256","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Sunburn","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The ship of characters Sunny (or Omori) and Aubrey from the videogame Omori."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Sunburn"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sunburn","blocks":[{"text":"Sunburn is a form of radiation burn that affects living tissue, such as skin, that results from an overexposure to ultraviolet (UV) radiation, usually from the Sun. Common symptoms in humans and other animals include red or reddish skin that is hot to the touch or painful, general fatigue, and mild dizziness. Other symptoms include blistering, peeling skin, swelling, itching, and nausea. Excessive UV radiation is the leading cause of (primarily) non-malignant skin tumors, which in extreme cases can be life-threatening. Sunburn is an inflammatory response in the tissue triggered by the nucleic acid damage caused by UV radiation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Sunburn_Treatment_Practices.jpg/330px-Sunburn_Treatment_Practices.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sunburn"},{"title":"Sunburn (Dominic Fike album)","blocks":[{"text":"Sunburn is the second studio album by American musician Dominic Fike, released through Sandy Boys and Columbia Records on July 7, 2023. The album was primarily produced by Jim-E Stack, Devin Workman, and Henry Kwapis."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/ac/Dominic_Fike_-_Sunburn.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sunburn_(Dominic_Fike_album)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Sunburn_blisters.jpg/500px-Sunburn_blisters.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Sunburn_blisters.jpg/1280px-Sunburn_blisters.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Sunburn_blisters.jpg/500px-Sunburn_blisters.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASunburn_blisters.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Sunburned_knee.png/500px-Sunburned_knee.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Sunburned_knee.png/1280px-Sunburned_knee.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Sunburned_knee.png/500px-Sunburned_knee.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASunburned_knee.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/UV_Diurnal_Erythemal_Dose_Rate_Per_Latitude_graph.png/500px-UV_Diurnal_Erythemal_Dose_Rate_Per_Latitude_graph.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/UV_Diurnal_Erythemal_Dose_Rate_Per_Latitude_graph.png/500px-UV_Diurnal_Erythemal_Dose_Rate_Per_Latitude_graph.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Erythemal dose rate at three Northern latitudes. (Divide by 25 to obtain the UV Index.) Source: NOAA.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AUV_Diurnal_Erythemal_Dose_Rate_Per_Latitude_graph.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Sun_burn.JPG/500px-Sun_burn.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Sun_burn.JPG/500px-Sun_burn.JPG?utm_source=en.wik